Set up Halfhand: create the data directory and a starter config.

Creates the data directory, database, blob store and exports directory, and writes a commented starter config.toml if no config file exists yet. Prints every path it created or found. Safe to run again: an existing config is never overwritten without --force. Optional: every other command sets up what it needs on first use.

Usage: hh init [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --force
          Recreate config.toml from the starter template, first saving the existing file as config.toml.bak

      --migrate-config
          Rename a legacy halfhand.toml (or hh.toml) to config.toml, the name Halfhand reads first. Does nothing if config.toml already exists

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Examples:
  hh init                   create the data dir and a starter config
  hh init --migrate-config  rename halfhand.toml to config.toml
  hh init --force           rewrite config.toml from the template (old one kept as .bak)

Docs: https://halfhand.org/docs/init/
